# Frontend (TS + pnpm + Vite + Pentatrion)

## Layout (REQ-ASSETS-001)

- TypeScript/React sources: `src/Resources/assets/src/`
- Production build output: `src/Resources/public/build/` (for `assets:install`)
- Root `package.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `vite.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`

## Commands

```bash
# Bundle production build (Packagist / host apps)
pnpm install && pnpm run build
# or
make assets

# Demo (Docker)
make -C demo/symfony8 up      # composer + assets-install + Pentatrion build
make -C demo/symfony8 assets  # rebuild Vite after TS changes
```

## Pentatrion (demo only)

- `pentatrion/vite-bundle` + `vite-plugin-symfony` in `demo/symfony8/`
- Entry: `demo/symfony8/assets/pdf-editor.ts` → imports `@bundle/src/main.tsx`
- Twig: `vite_entry_link_tags('pdf-editor')` / `vite_entry_script_tags('pdf-editor')`
- Portable bundle Twig keeps `asset('build/pdf-editor.js', 'nowo_pdf_editor')` for hosts without Pentatrion

## Do not

- Move frontend back under a loose `assets/` folder at repo root
- Hardcode demo-only paths in `src/Resources/assets/` (keep portable)
- Change Vite `base` in root config without updating Symfony asset package path
